## Steer-4 — auth enforcement, atomic money, typed errors, domain modules (2026-09-04)

### A1 — The contract now enforces its own access metadata (blocker fixed)

- `services/billing/src/auth.ts` + `services/runs/src/auth.ts`: `createContractAuthorizer`
  projects the declared `authentication`/`scopes`/`roles` onto the real REST+RPC mounts; the
  authenticator maps env-injected bearer tokens (Aspire-injected dev tokens) to principals and
  fails closed — a missing env simply registers no credential.
- `defineService({ auth: { authn, authz } })` wired in both services; `/health` stays public,
  everything under `/api` is guarded.
- Every `?? 'api'` fallback deleted: `requireActor()` narrows the principal and throws
  UNAUTHORIZED when absent — audit rows record real subjects now.

### A2 — Money mutations are atomic (blocker fixed)

- `defineService({ db })` injects the Postgres client; `postgresOf(context.db)` narrows it once
  with a runtime check (`DbContext` is typed `object` by the framework). All `db.getClient()`
  singleton sites replaced; `/health` now probes the DB.
- `withIdempotency` moved to `services/_shared/idempotency.ts` and made transactional: the
  guarded operation runs inside ONE transaction that also commits the stored response, so a
  crash can never leave a SUCCEEDED payment against an OPEN invoice (the steer's exact
  silent-loss scenario). Failures store outside the rolled-back tx so same-key retries replay
  the same failure (Stripe semantics).
- `withTransaction` wraps: `issueInvoice`, `voidInvoice`, `payInvoice` (via idempotency tx),
  `applyPlanChange` (Serializable), `customers.create`, `creditNotes.create` (via idempotency tx),
  `createSubscription`, `stagePlanChange`, `decideRunItem`, `computeRun` state flips.

### A3 — Errors speak the contract's vocabulary

- `services/*/routers/raise.ts`: domain errors → `errors.NOT_FOUND` (404, structured
  resourceType/resourceId data), `errors.CONFLICT` (409 — declared on the idempotency-guarded
  procedures pay/creditNotes/issue via procedure `.errors()`), `errors.VALIDATION_ERROR` (422)
  for state-machine violations. Unknown errors still 500 (genuine faults).
- `BillingErrorEnvelopeSchemaV1` deleted.

### A4 — Domain modules + one money seam

- New domain modules: `customers` (list/search/detail aggregates/create), `plans` (+meters),
  `credit` (credit notes/ledger/entitlements); the invoice-detail projection deduplicated into
  `serializeInvoiceDetail` (was copy-pasted 4×).
- `services/_shared/money.ts` is the single seam: `toDb`/`fromDb` are the ONLY Decimal↔string
  conversions; the third rounding copy (runs) deleted. Exact-percent delta rewritten on money
  micros instead of floats.
- `buildSearchCondition` adopted for customer search. `offsetPaginatedQuery` NOT adopted: its
  `PrismaModelDelegate` structurally rejects the Deno-generated client's delegates
  (contravariance on `args?: unknown`) and passing one requires a type escape — recorded as a
  framework type-friction finding; the zero-escape bar wins. Envelope schemas keep plain zod
  pagination for the same reason (helpers' `ContractSchema` degrades oRPC-inferred handler
  input to `{}` — probe evidence from steer-2).

### A5 — Negative-authorization tests (the bar's "test file, not a curl transcript")

- `tests/negative-auth_test.ts`: 19 in-process assertions driving the REAL billing/runs apps
  (production auth modules + contract authorizers, `ServiceApp.fetch()`): unauthenticated →
  401 on every guarded resource; usage-only credential → 403 on billing reads; operator
  (no finance:admin role) → 403 on void; runs:read-only credential → 403 on create/decide;
  bogus tokens → 401; contract health procedures public → 200; the old doubled path denied.
- LIVE proof (AppHost restarted with the new wiring): `/api/invoices` 401 without token →
  403 with the usage-only token → 200 with the operator token; runs same. The triple is real.

## Steer-5 — hardcoded `/api/v1` stripped (defect + lesson)

`find_guidance("declare the route path and version prefix ... without hardcoding /api/v1")`
answered with confidence high BEFORE the edit: the REST mount adds `/api` at runtime and the
canonical contract carries resource paths only (`/workspace/{workspace}/members`); the version
lives in the file layout (`contracts/versions/v1/`) and the RPC mount (`/api/rpc/v1/<service>`).
All 31 routes stripped (`/invoices`, `/runs/{id}/compute`, …) and verified live: the served path
is `/api/invoices` (200 with the operator token) — no doubled prefix.

### MCP ledger — steer-4/5 lookups and what each changed

1. `find_guidance` "createContractAuthorizer withAuthz defineService auth" → the opt-in
   enforcement switch + `createStaticCredentialAuthenticator` credential model (A1).
2. Reference page `services-sdk/services` `defineService` options → the `db` (context.db) and
   `auth` option keys (A1/A2).
3. `deno doc @netscript/service/auth` → authenticator/authorizer port shapes; `@netscript/sdk/client`
   docs + the "typed bearer credentials" doc section → `createBearerSdkClientContribution`
   attached to the runs→billing client (explicit `TContributions` tuple parameter required —
   inference from the literal alone fails type-check, recorded).
4. `deno doc @netscript/contracts/query` → `buildSearchCondition` adopted; `offsetPaginatedQuery`
   rejected with evidence (see A4).
5. `deno doc @netscript/database` → `withTransaction(client, fn, { isolationLevel })` (A2).
6. Runtime probes of the pinned error map → 404/422 data shapes; procedure-level `.errors()`
   accepts a CONFLICT definition (A3).
7. `deno doc @netscript/service` ServiceApp → `fetch()`/`request()` in-memory surface the
   negative-auth suite drives (A5).
8. `find_guidance` "route path and version prefix" (steer-5, asked BEFORE the edit per the new
   hard rule) → the mount adds `/api`; version is file/RPC-level, not path-level.
